Precedence of the render settings resolution over the host framing, see test_2819 and #2819

A sphere is rendered with a zoom framing, then a film translate framing, while the host sets and clears the render
settings resolution. With a resolution, the host framing is ignored as before the support of the framing (this is what
husk relies on), and clearing the resolution makes the framing apply again.
The scenario only runs with the HdArnoldRendererPlugin render delegate driven like a Hydra host, see
testsuite/common/interactive_usd_test.h. Each render is checked in test.cpp, and the last one is compared against the
reference image.

author: cyril.pichard

PARAMS: {'program_env': 'interactive_usd'}
